messages:
Sonia (Partners): Heads-up28094were planning a compatibility change for partner-facing API: were renaming the auth header and flattening the response context. We need marketplace resubmission, firmware/SDK checks from hardware partners, and SI release notes. 5-6 week runway suggested. Who takes announcement + migration docs?

Evan M: Can you paste a minimal before/after so SDKs can scope impact? Also does this affect streaming endpoints or just sync responses?

Sonia (Partners): Minimal diff below. Affects sync + streaming meta headers.

```json
// existing envelope
{ "context": { "req_id": "r-123", "region": "us-west" }, "result": {...} }

// new envelope
{ "req_id": "r-123", "zone": "us-west-2", "service_hint": "micro", "result": {...} }

// header change
X-RW-Auth: token -> X-RW-Auth-v2: token
```

Lena K: For Dedicated/private we cannot break existing customers. Recommend: 1) add a server-side compatibility shim that emits v2 headers on demand, 2) feature-flag per-tenant for rollout, 3) telemetry event when shim is used. I can take the shim work.

Ravi S: SDK plan: ship minor releases that detect the new envelope and map fields for older user code. Ill add auto-detect + opt-in enforcement. ETA: initial PRs in 8 business days. Example Node snippet Ill include: 

```js
// autodetect and normalize
const resp = await client.call(...);
if (resp.req_id && !resp.context) {
  // normalize to old shape for apps expecting context
  resp.context = { req_id: resp.req_id, region: resp.zone };
}
```

Tom B: Ops requests: we need a canary plan and clear rollback thresholds. Suggest 0.5% -> 2.5% staged canary over 10 days, monitor 4xx auth failures and error-rate delta. Auto-rollback if auth failures > 0.5% absolute or latency P95 increases > 40ms.

MarketplaceBot: Marketplace resubmission earliest slot 2026-08-04; standard review 3 business days. Include compatibility note and migration guide in submission.

Evan M: Partner outreach list: CloudMarket, Ionix Systems, EdgeWorks, IntegrateFast, AccelSys. Hardware partners will need firmware/SDK compatibility validation (expect ~2 weeks for partner QA). We should ask partners to run a small test harness. I can own the harness.

Sonia (Partners): Action owners so far: Shim/runtime adapter (Lena), SDK releases + migration snippets (Ravi), Canary + runbook (Tom), Partner test harness + outreach (Evan), Partner signoffs + embargo (Sonia). Priya from PR will need the copy for embargoed partner comms.

Ravi S: Migration docs checklist: 1) quick diff, 2) code samples for Node/Python/Go, 3) environment variable to force v2/v3 for testing, 4) telemetry events for deprecation. Short Python example: 

```python
# normalize v3->v2
resp = client.call(...)
if "req_id" in resp and "context" not in resp:
    resp["context"] = {"req_id": resp.pop("req_id"), "region": resp.pop("zone", None)}
```

Tom B: I'll draft the canary runbook: objectives, metrics (auth failures, error-rate, latency P95), rollout steps, partner verification checklist, auto-rollback conditions, slack alerting, pager thresholds.

Evan M: Partner test harness will include: curl/HTTP examples, small replay tool, and a checksum comparison for normalized payloads. Will ship to partners as a repo + GH action. Request partner QA window of 10 business days.

Sonia (Partners): Proposed timeline: Week 0: partner outreach + embargo request. Week 1-2: SDK + shim PRs + partner harness. Week 3: internal canary (0.5% -> 1%). Week 4: partner QA window. Week 5-6: ramp + public announcement and marketplace resubmission. Any objections?

Lena K: No objections. I'll include an admin console toggle per-tenant and a 90-day compatibility mode for those who need it.

Ravi S: Will add deprecation telemetry and a migration example page. Also will publish a short FAQ for common migration questions.

Tom B: Reminder: include SRE runbook snippets for emergency switchback and a quick curl to force legacy envelope for a tenant. Example curl: 

```bash
curl -H "X-RW-Auth-v2: TOKEN" -H "Accept: application/json" https://api.redwood.example/partner/endpoint
```

MarketplaceBot: Note: include a short line in the marketplace submission about "backwards-compatible adapter available for customers; partners may opt-in to new envelope" for faster approval.

Sonia (Partners): Great. I'll open the shared tracker and notify legal for embargo paperwork. Please add your PR links and ETA into the tracker by EOD. If no objections, I'll start outreach this afternoon. :thumbsup:
